Examples for the KIARA galaxy formation model:

 - MAGMA2 SPH,
 - KIARA cooling (built-in crackle: primordial and metal-line cooling,
   H2, dust formation and destruction, interstellar radiation field),
 - KIARA chemistry (11 elements, metal diffusion, firehose wind mixing),
 - KIARA star formation and stellar feedback (chem5 yields, decoupled
   kinetic winds),
 - Obsidian black holes (Rennehan et al. 2024).

Shared files:

 - chem5/             chem5 stellar lifetime and yield tables (KIARAFeedback:tables_path)
 - getCloudyTable.sh  fetches the Cloudy table used by the cooling (KIARACooling:cloudy_table)

Star particle luminosities (the Luminosities output) are only computed if
Stars:luminosity_filename points to the EAGLE photometry tables (see
../EAGLE_ICs/getEaglePhotometryTable.sh); the examples do not set it.

Examples:

 - KIARA_25/          EAGLE 25 Mpc ICs at low resolution (L0025N0188), with the
                      current KIARA calibration.
